fields.description:
Noticed this while I was documenting the feature. This was fixed during a prior iteration of the enrol/lti code, but I removed it since at the time I thought it wasn't having any effect. In fact it was, and I was silly to remove it.

enrol/lti/styles.css needs the following:
{code:java}#registration-tab-content .input-group-append a.btn span.pix {
    padding-left: 0.5rem;
} {code}
to ensure the spacing on either side of the pix icon is even.

Without the fix:

!uneven_icon_spacing.png|thumbnail!

With the fix:

!fixed_icon_spacing.png|thumbnail!

Reported here: [https://moodle.org/mod/forum/discuss.php?d=432562]

Line 55:
{code:java}
 $table->add_key('unique_key', XMLDB_KEY_UNIQUE, ['userid, issuer256, sub256']);{code}
Shouldn't quote all fields in one string, but rather should quote the individual fields. This presents as an upgrade error on sqlsrv (and perhaps other dbs).

I.e. should be doing this:


{code:java}
$table->add_key('unique_key', XMLDB_KEY_UNIQUE, ['userid', 'issuer256', 'sub256']); {code}

Postgres seems to work somehow - as if that code path corrects the index or something.
Mariadb - works and index created ok - same as pgsql.
Mysql - works and index created ok - same as pgsql.
Oracle - fails upgrade like mssql does.
